Testbench
1. Objective

The purpose of the testbench is to verify that the Women Safety IoT Device correctly responds to emergency conditions and handles GPS and GSM communication.

2. Test Environment
Hardware

ESP32

SOS push button

Buzzer

LED

GPS module

GSM module

Software

Arduino IDE

ESP32 board package

TinyGPS++ library

Serial Monitor

3. Test Cases
TC01 – Power-On Test

Input:

Power ON the ESP32.

Expected result:

ESP32 starts successfully.

LED is OFF.

Buzzer is OFF.

Serial Monitor displays system initialization.

System enters monitoring mode.

Expected output:

Women Safety IoT Device
GSM initialized.
System ready.

TC02 – Normal Operation

Input:

Do not press the SOS button.

Expected result:

No emergency alarm.

Buzzer remains OFF.

Device continues monitoring.

Expected output:

System ready.

TC03 – SOS Button Test

Input:

Press the SOS button.

Expected result:

Emergency mode starts.

Buzzer turns ON/OFF.

LED begins blinking.

Emergency message is generated.

Expected output:

!!! EMERGENCY !!!
SOS button activated.

TC04 – GPS Available

Input:

Press SOS while valid GPS data is available.

Expected result:

The generated message contains latitude and longitude.

Example:

EMERGENCY ALERT!
SOS button activated.

Latitude: 15.828125
Longitude: 78.037270

Google Maps:
https://maps.google.com/?q=15.828125,78.037270

TC05 – GPS Unavailable

Input:

Press SOS without a valid GPS fix.

Expected result:

The emergency system still activates.

Expected message:

EMERGENCY ALERT!
SOS button activated.

GPS location unavailable.


The lack of GPS data should not prevent the local alarm from operating.

TC06 – GSM SMS Test

Input:

Press SOS with GSM network available.

Expected result:

The GSM module receives the SMS command and sends the emergency message.

Serial output:

Sending SMS...
SMS command completed.

TC07 – GSM Unavailable

Input:

Press SOS while GSM communication is unavailable.

Expected result:

Local buzzer continues operating.

LED continues indicating emergency mode.

System does not stop because of GSM failure.

TC08 – Multiple Button Presses

Input:

Press SOS repeatedly.

Expected result:

The system remains in emergency mode and does not repeatedly trigger a new emergency SMS on every loop iteration.

